/*
 * One counter per chip-1 channel strip, incremented by the SPI
 * handler on every accepted write into that strip's 144-word page,
 * plus a catch-all slot for everything outside the strip pages.
 *
 * A node preps its control state when the counter differs from the
 * epoch it last prepped at, or while it (or a node it depends on) is
 * running a ramp. Readers never write these words, so a strip can
 * carry any number of watchers without a clear-race.
 *
 * CHIP 1 ONLY. Chip 2 assembles this file too -- everything under
 * src/ is assembled once per chip -- but its nodes are not
 * strip-shaped, none of them gate on an epoch, and the fader-busy
 * pointer table below names chip-1 symbols that do not exist in a
 * chip-2 link. So the whole body is behind CHIP_ID == 1.
 *
 * INITIALISED TO 1, and the node-side "last seen" words to 0, so every
 * gated node preps on the first block after reset whatever the host
 * has or has not written.
 */

